From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin Raevsky <valentin@compulab.co.il>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: maxim-serdes: discover optional camera links

A static four-port camera profile must not fail deserializer probe when
only a subset of the camera assemblies is connected. Prune unlocked GMSL
inputs after enabling POC power and before publishing I2C adapters or V4L2
async sources. Try every advertised link rate, but treat only link-lock
timeouts as absence; local bus and register failures remain fatal.

Keep source stream and output virtual channel equal to the physical input
index for the opt-in profile. The normal first-free allocator otherwise
compacts sparse camera subsets and no longer matches the fixed NVIDIA
NVCSI/VI channels. Validate that each optional input carries one native
VC0 sensor stream and leave ordinary routing unchanged.

Use one configured serializer alias per physical input instead of a
shared first-free pool. When preparing an isolated link, also check the
explicitly configured aliases so a warm camera moved between ports can
be recovered and readdressed without scanning arbitrary I2C addresses.

Detach only referenced absent NVIDIA camera-module metadata subtrees from
the live device tree before async registration. A status property alone
does not guarantee that the closed Argus parser ignores absent modules.
Queue metadata children before their parents, so managed changeset
reversion reattaches parents first on failed probe or driver removal.
Never alter sensor nodes or public SerDes structures.

This is boot-time discovery for known camera assemblies, not arbitrary
sensor-model detection or runtime hotplug. The no-camera configuration is
valid and leaves no upstream camera sources. CONFIG_OF_DYNAMIC is required
only by the opt-in profile.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CompuLab EDGEDES optional-camera profile]
Signed-off-by: Valentin Raevsky <valentin@compulab.co.il>
---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/maxim,max96712.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/maxim,max96712.yaml
index fe35f9d..c132638 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/maxim,max96712.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/maxim,max96712.yaml
@@ -48,6 +48,47 @@ properties:
       Without this local option, initialize only the first enabled input.
     type: boolean
 
+  compulab,allow-missing-links:
+    description: |
+      Discover connected camera assemblies at probe time after POC power
+      is enabled. Try each supported GMSL2 rate and omit input links that
+      never lock, without registering their I2C adapters or async sources.
+      Local I2C and register failures still abort probe. This is not a
+      runtime hotplug interface or automatic sensor-model detection.
+      Each camera must supply one native VC0 stream. The physical input
+      index remains its source stream and output VC, even when other
+      inputs are absent. Requires multi-link default routing and a kernel
+      with CONFIG_OF_DYNAMIC to update the NVIDIA camera metadata.
+    type: boolean
+
+  compulab,camera-modules:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle-array
+    description: |
+      NVIDIA tegra-camera-platform/modules/module0 through module3
+      metadata nodes in physical GMSL input order. Missing camera modules
+      and their metadata children are detached from the live tree before
+      async registration, so userspace cannot enumerate absent sensors.
+      The changeset is reverted on driver removal or failed probe.
+      Only metadata without a compatible property may be referenced.
+    minItems: 4
+    maxItems: 4
+
+  compulab,serializer-aliases:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-array
+    description: |
+      One unique 7-bit serializer alias per physical GMSL input, in port
+      order. Unlike first-free allocation from the shared pool, these
+      aliases remain fixed for any connected-camera subset. The isolated
+      link also probes these configured aliases to recover a warm camera
+      moved from another input, then readdresses it to its current alias.
+      Aliases must not equal the deserializer's own I2C address.
+    minItems: 4
+    maxItems: 4
+    uniqueItems: true
+    items:
+      minimum: 8
+      maximum: 119
+
   maxim,control-channel-port:
     description:
       Selects which deserializer control-channel port is connected to the
@@ -144,6 +185,13 @@ allOf:
 dependentRequired:
   i2c-atr: [i2c-alias-pool]
   i2c-alias-pool: [i2c-atr]
+  compulab,allow-missing-links:
+    - compulab,default-multi-link-routes
+    - compulab,camera-modules
+    - compulab,serializer-aliases
+    - i2c-atr
+  compulab,camera-modules: ["compulab,allow-missing-links"]
+  compulab,serializer-aliases: ["compulab,allow-missing-links"]
 
 examples:
   - |
diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/maxim-serdes/max_des.c b/drivers/media/i2c/maxim-serdes/max_des.c
index 036bdc8..68cfecf 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/maxim-serdes/max_des.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/maxim-serdes/max_des.c
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 #include <linux/i2c-atr.h>
 #include <linux/i2c-mux.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/property.h>
 #include <linux/regulator/consumer.h>
 #include <linux/sched.h>
@@ -52,6 +53,11 @@ struct max_des_priv {
 	struct v4l2_ctrl_handler ctrl_handler;
 
 	struct max_des_phy *unused_phy;
+	bool allow_missing_links;
+	u16 serializer_aliases[MAX_DES_NUM_LINKS];
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_OF_DYNAMIC)
+	struct of_changeset camera_modules_changeset;
+#endif
 };
 
 struct max_des_remap_context {
@@ -390,20 +396,33 @@ static int max_des_set_pipe_vc_remaps(struct max_des_priv *priv,
 
 static int max_des_map_src_dst_vc_id(struct max_des_remap_context *context,
 				     unsigned int pipe_id, unsigned int phy_id,
-				     unsigned int src_vc_id, bool keep_vc)
+				     unsigned int src_vc_id, bool keep_vc,
+				     int preferred_dst_vc)
 {
 	unsigned int vc_id;
 
 	if (src_vc_id >= MAX_SERDES_VC_ID_NUM)
 		return -E2BIG;
 
-	if (context->vc_ids_masks[pipe_id][phy_id] & BIT(src_vc_id))
+	if (context->vc_ids_masks[pipe_id][phy_id] & BIT(src_vc_id)) {
+		if (preferred_dst_vc >= 0 &&
+		    context->vc_ids_map[pipe_id][phy_id][src_vc_id] !=
+		    (unsigned int)preferred_dst_vc)
+			return -EINVAL;
 		return 0;
+	}
 
-	if (keep_vc && !(context->dst_vc_ids_masks[phy_id] & BIT(src_vc_id)))
+	if (preferred_dst_vc >= 0) {
+		if (preferred_dst_vc >= MAX_SERDES_VC_ID_NUM)
+			return -E2BIG;
+		if (context->dst_vc_ids_masks[phy_id] & BIT(preferred_dst_vc))
+			return -EINVAL;
+		vc_id = preferred_dst_vc;
+	} else if (keep_vc && !(context->dst_vc_ids_masks[phy_id] & BIT(src_vc_id))) {
 		vc_id = src_vc_id;
-	else
+	} else {
 		vc_id = ffz(context->dst_vc_ids_masks[phy_id]);
+	}
 
 	if (vc_id != src_vc_id)
 		context->vc_ids_remapped[pipe_id] = true;
@@ -590,8 +609,19 @@ static int max_des_populate_remap_context(struct max_des_priv *priv,
 
 		keep_vc = max_des_should_keep_vc(priv, &hw, modes);
 
+		/* This opt-in profile carries one native VC0 sensor per port. */
+		if (priv->allow_missing_links &&
+		    (hw.is_tpg || route->sink_stream ||
+		     route->sink_pad >= priv->des->info->num_links ||
+		     route->source_stream != route->sink_pad ||
+		     route->source_stream >= MAX_SERDES_VC_ID_NUM ||
+		     hw.entry.bus.csi2.vc))
+			return -EINVAL;
+
 		ret = max_des_map_src_dst_vc_id(context, hw.pipe->index, hw.phy->index,
-						hw.entry.bus.csi2.vc, keep_vc);
+						hw.entry.bus.csi2.vc, keep_vc,
+						priv->allow_missing_links ?
+						(int)route->source_stream : -1);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
 	}
@@ -1389,7 +1419,9 @@ static int max_des_init_link_ser_xlate(struct max_des_priv *priv,
 				       u8 power_up_addr, u8 new_addr)
 {
 	struct max_des *des = priv->des;
-	u8 addrs[] = { power_up_addr, new_addr };
+	u8 addrs[MAX_DES_NUM_LINKS + 2] = { power_up_addr, new_addr };
+	unsigned int num_addrs = 2;
+	unsigned int i;
 	bool preserve_gmsl2;
 	bool reset_done;
 	u8 current_addr;
@@ -1401,7 +1433,16 @@ static int max_des_init_link_ser_xlate(struct max_des_priv *priv,
 			return ret;
 	}
 
-	ret = max_ser_wait_for_multiple(adapter, addrs, ARRAY_SIZE(addrs),
+	/* A warm camera moved to another port can retain its old alias. */
+	if (priv->allow_missing_links) {
+		for (i = 0; i < des->info->num_links; i++) {
+			u8 alias = priv->serializer_aliases[i];
+
+			if (alias != power_up_addr && alias != new_addr)
+				addrs[num_addrs++] = alias;
+		}
+	}
+	ret = max_ser_wait_for_multiple(adapter, addrs, num_addrs,
 					&current_addr);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(priv->dev,
@@ -1700,6 +1741,10 @@ static int max_des_i2c_atr_init(struct max_des_priv *priv)
 		if (!link->enabled)
 			continue;
 
+		if (priv->allow_missing_links) {
+			desc.num_aliases = 1;
+			desc.aliases = &priv->serializer_aliases[i];
+		}
 		ret = i2c_atr_add_adapter(priv->atr, &desc);
 		if (ret)
 			goto err_add_adapters;
@@ -2604,7 +2649,7 @@ static int max_des_init_state(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
 			.sink_pad = max_des_link_to_pad(des, link),
 			.sink_stream = 0,
 			.source_pad = max_des_phy_to_pad(des, phy),
-			.source_stream = stream,
+			.source_stream = priv->allow_missing_links ? link->index : stream,
 			.flags = V4L2_SUBDEV_ROUTE_FL_ACTIVE,
 		};
 		stream++;
@@ -2949,6 +2994,158 @@ err_rollback:
 	return ret;
 }
 
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_OF_DYNAMIC)
+static int max_des_detach_camera_module(struct of_changeset *ocs,
+					struct device_node *node)
+{
+	struct device_node *child;
+	int ret;
+
+	/* This changeset is for Argus metadata, not instantiated devices. */
+	if (of_find_property(node, "compatible", NULL))
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	for_each_child_of_node(node, child) {
+		ret = max_des_detach_camera_module(ocs, child);
+		if (ret) {
+			of_node_put(child);
+			return ret;
+		}
+	}
+
+	/* Reverting the changeset must reattach parents before children. */
+	return of_changeset_detach_node(ocs, node);
+}
+
+static void max_des_restore_camera_modules(void *data)
+{
+	struct max_des_priv *priv = data;
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = of_changeset_revert(&priv->camera_modules_changeset);
+	if (ret)
+		dev_warn(priv->dev, "Failed to restore camera metadata: %d\n", ret);
+	of_changeset_destroy(&priv->camera_modules_changeset);
+}
+
+static int max_des_update_camera_modules(struct max_des_priv *priv)
+{
+	struct of_changeset *ocs = &priv->camera_modules_changeset;
+	struct max_des *des = priv->des;
+	unsigned int i;
+	int ret;
+
+	if (!priv->allow_missing_links)
+		return 0;
+
+	of_changeset_init(ocs);
+	for (i = 0; i < des->info->num_links; i++) {
+		struct device_node *node, *parent, *platform;
+		char name[12];
+		bool valid;
+
+		node = of_parse_phandle(priv->dev->of_node,
+					"compulab,camera-modules", i);
+		if (!node) {
+			ret = -EINVAL;
+			goto err_destroy;
+		}
+		parent = of_get_parent(node);
+		platform = of_get_parent(parent);
+		snprintf(name, sizeof(name), "module%u", i);
+		valid = of_node_name_eq(node, name) &&
+			of_node_name_eq(parent, "modules") &&
+			of_node_name_eq(platform, "tegra-camera-platform");
+		of_node_put(platform);
+		of_node_put(parent);
+		if (!valid) {
+			of_node_put(node);
+			ret = -EINVAL;
+			goto err_destroy;
+		}
+		ret = des->links[i].enabled ? 0 :
+			max_des_detach_camera_module(ocs, node);
+		of_node_put(node);
+		if (ret)
+			goto err_destroy;
+	}
+
+	if (list_empty(&ocs->entries)) {
+		of_changeset_destroy(ocs);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
+	ret = of_changeset_apply(ocs);
+	if (ret)
+		goto err_destroy;
+
+	return devm_add_action_or_reset(priv->dev,
+				       max_des_restore_camera_modules, priv);
+
+err_destroy:
+	of_changeset_destroy(ocs);
+	return ret;
+}
+#else
+static int max_des_update_camera_modules(struct max_des_priv *priv)
+{
+	return priv->allow_missing_links ? -EOPNOTSUPP : 0;
+}
+#endif
+
+static int max_des_detect_connected_links(struct max_des_priv *priv)
+{
+	struct max_des *des = priv->des;
+	unsigned int i;
+	int version, ret;
+
+	if (!priv->allow_missing_links)
+		return 0;
+	if (!des->ops->select_links)
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < des->info->num_links; i++) {
+		struct max_des_link *link = &des->links[i];
+
+		if (!link->enabled)
+			continue;
+
+		ret = -ETIMEDOUT;
+		for (version = MAX_SERDES_GMSL_MAX;
+		     version >= MAX_SERDES_GMSL_MIN; version--) {
+			if (!(des->info->versions & BIT(version)))
+				continue;
+			if (des->ops->set_link_version) {
+				ret = des->ops->set_link_version(des, link, version);
+				if (ret)
+					return ret;
+			}
+			ret = des->ops->select_links(des, BIT(link->index));
+			if (!ret) {
+				link->version = version;
+				break;
+			}
+			/* A local bus/register failure is not an absent camera. */
+			if (ret != -ETIMEDOUT)
+				return ret;
+		}
+		if (!ret)
+			continue;
+
+		/* Balance the POC reference before the normal cleanup skips it. */
+		if (priv->pocs[i]) {
+			ret = regulator_disable(priv->pocs[i]);
+			if (ret)
+				return ret;
+		}
+		link->enabled = false;
+		dev_info(priv->dev, "GMSL port %u: no camera connected\n", i);
+	}
+
+	/* An empty camera profile is valid: leave all links disabled. */
+	return des->ops->select_links(des, max_des_enabled_links_mask(des));
+}
+
 static int max_des_parse_sink_dt_endpoint(struct max_des_priv *priv,
 					  struct max_des_link *link,
 					  struct max_serdes_source *source,
@@ -3261,6 +3458,8 @@ int max_des_probe(struct i2c_client *client, struct max_des *des)
 {
 	struct device *dev = &client->dev;
 	struct max_des_priv *priv;
+	u32 aliases[MAX_DES_NUM_LINKS];
+	unsigned int i, j;
 	int ret;
 
 	if (des->info->num_phys > MAX_DES_NUM_PHYS)
@@ -3300,6 +3499,31 @@ int max_des_probe(struct i2c_client *client, struct max_des *des)
 	priv->dev = dev;
 	priv->des = des;
 	des->priv = priv;
+	priv->allow_missing_links =
+		device_property_read_bool(dev, "compulab,allow-missing-links");
+	if (priv->allow_missing_links) {
+		if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_OF_DYNAMIC) || !dev->of_node)
+			return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+		if (!device_property_read_bool(dev, "compulab,default-multi-link-routes") ||
+		    of_count_phandle_with_args(dev->of_node, "compulab,camera-modules", NULL) !=
+		    des->info->num_links ||
+		    device_property_count_u32(dev, "compulab,serializer-aliases") !=
+		    des->info->num_links)
+			return -EINVAL;
+		ret = device_property_read_u32_array(dev, "compulab,serializer-aliases",
+						     aliases, des->info->num_links);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+		for (i = 0; i < des->info->num_links; i++) {
+			if (aliases[i] < 0x08 || aliases[i] > 0x77 ||
+			    aliases[i] == client->addr)
+				return -EINVAL;
+			for (j = 0; j < i; j++)
+				if (aliases[i] == aliases[j])
+					return -EINVAL;
+			priv->serializer_aliases[i] = aliases[i];
+		}
+	}
 
 	ret = max_des_allocate(priv);
 	if (ret)
@@ -3317,6 +3541,14 @@ int max_des_probe(struct i2c_client *client, struct max_des *des)
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_put_source_ep_fwnodes;
 
+	ret = max_des_detect_connected_links(priv);
+	if (ret)
+		goto err_disable_pocs;
+
+	ret = max_des_update_camera_modules(priv);
+	if (ret)
+		goto err_disable_pocs;
+
 	ret = max_des_i2c_adapter_init(priv);
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_disable_pocs;
-- 
2.34.1

